    "ecom_faq_9JNHQA": {
      "type": "ecom-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "question_Xa8UUH": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "category": "product",
            "title": "How does Lio work if there's no nicotine?",
            "content": "<p>Your bad habit are two addictions: the nicotine, and the ritual.</p><p>Patches handle the nicotine. But they leave you with empty hands, still craving the motion, the breath, the throat hit, the ritual you've repeated 10,000 times.</p><p>Lio handles the ritual half.</p><p>Same hand-to-mouth motion. Same deep breathing pattern. Same throat sensation and flavor. Your brain gets the sensory signals it's craving, your body gets clean air.</p><p><strong>100,000+ people have quit this way.</strong> Not magic, just finally addressing both halves of the problem.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_ipPnxK": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "category": "product",
            "title": "What does flavored air taste like?",
            "content": "<p>If you’re used to vapor, Lio might feel lighter at first, but it’s designed for a healthier future. Think of Lio as herbal tea compared to the sticky soda of vapor: less intense, more natural, and far better for you.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_BE4wCE": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "category": "product",
            "title": "What are Lio cores made of?",
            "content": "<p>Plant extracts. That's it.</p><p><strong>What's in it:</strong></p><ul><li>Essential oils (peppermint, eucalyptus, cinnamon)</li><li>Natural plant extracts for flavor</li><li>Food-grade vegetable glycerin (same stuff in toothpaste)</li></ul><p><strong>What's NOT in it:</strong><br/>No nicotine. No tobacco. No chemicals. No batteries. No heating. Nothing artificial.</p><p>The same essential oils used in aromatherapy clinics for decades - just engineered to replace your smoking ritual instead of relaxing you on a spa table.</p><p>Every batch is third-party tested.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_fKTip9": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "category": "product",
            "title": "Is Lio safe to use?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. You're inhaling plant-based essential oils and clean air. The same essential oils used safely in aromatherapy for decades.</p><p></p><p>No nicotine. No tobacco. No heating elements creating toxic byproducts. No combustion. No chemicals.</p><p></p><p>Every batch is third-party tested. We're regulated as an aromatherapy device, not a smoking product.</p><p></p><p><strong>The real safety question:</strong> Is it safer than smoking? Absolutely. Is it safer than vaping? Yes - no batteries, no mysterious vape lung risks. Is it safer than patches? Same level, different approach.</p><p></p><p>You're trading poison for plants. That's the safety story.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_FBPU7q": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "category": "product",
            "title": "What if it doesn't work for me?",
            "content": "<p>Then you get your money back. Simple.</p><p><strong>30-day money-back guarantee. No questions asked.</strong></p><p>Try Lio for a full month. If you're not satisfied, if your cravings haven't decreased, if you genuinely gave it a shot and it didn't work - full refund.</p><p>You're not risking €49. You're risking 30 days to find out if you can finally quit.</p><p><strong>Here's the real question:</strong> How much have you already spent on cigarettes this month? How much will you spend next month if you do nothing?</p><p>The risk isn't trying Lio. The risk is staying where you are.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_VNNkNF": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "category": "product",
            "title": "Can I use Lio anywhere?",
            "content": "<p>Everywhere cigarettes are banned.</p><p>Planes. Restaurants. Your office. Inside your house. Sitting next to your kids.</p><p>No smoke. No vapor. No smell. No rules against breathing flavored air.</p><p>Nobody looks at you weird. Nobody asks you to step outside. Nobody makes you stand in the rain like a social outcast.</p><p><strong>You get your ritual back without the exile.</strong></p>"
          }
        },
        "question_dwmDxN": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "category": "product",
            "title": "How often can I use Lio?",
            "content": "<p>As often as you need.</p><p>Seriously - use it every time you'd normally reach for a cigarette. That's the entire point. You're replacing the ritual, not rationing it.</p><p><strong>Here's what actually happens:</strong></p><ul><li>Week 1: You're using it constantly (that's fine, you're rewiring 15 years of habits)</li><li>Week 2-3: Usage naturally starts dropping</li><li>Month 2+: Most people forget about it during the day</li></ul><p><em>\"Using less over time... mostly forget about it during the day now.\"</em></p><p>You're not trading one addiction for another. You're using a bridge to get to the other side. The bridge doesn't become your new prison - it's just how you cross.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_i9XGgg": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "category": "product",
            "title": "How long do Lio cores last?",
            "content": "<p>Each core lasts 3-5 days depending on how often you use it.</p><p><strong>Real-world math:</strong></p><ul><li>Journey Pack (6 cores) = 18-30 days</li><li>Freedom Pack (12 cores) = 36-60 days</li><li>Unstoppable Pack (16 cores) = 48-80 days</li></ul><p><strong>Compare that to smoking:</strong></p><ul><li>Pack-a-day = €300/month</li><li>Lio = €49-79 one-time, lasts 1-2 months</li></ul><p>You'll save money within the first week. Everything after that is just breathing easier - literally and financially.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_7QQR8i": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "category": "product",
            "title": "Will this work for someone as addicted as me?",
            "content": "<p>You think you're too far gone. Pack-a-day for 20 years. Chain smoker. Tried to quit 10 times and failed every time.</p><p>Here's what you need to hear: <strong>You're not the exception. You're the norm.</strong></p><p>Our average customer has:</p><ul><li>Smoked for 15-30 years</li><li>Tried quitting 3-7 times before</li><li>Been told they \"just need more willpower\"</li></ul><p><em>\"60 years old, smoked since I was a teenager. Tried many times, always failed. Lio worked.\"</em></p><p><em>\"Chain smoking, electric shisha, even tried for sugar cravings - this little thing helped me cut down almost completely. Day 14 now.\"</em></p><p>The people who think they're \"too addicted\" are exactly who this works for. Because you're not fighting chemistry with willpower anymore - you're replacing one ritual with another.</p><p><strong>Your brain doesn't care how long you've smoked. It just wants the pattern back.</strong> Lio gives it that.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_x3ta3q": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "category": "product",
            "title": "I've tried patches, gum, and vaping. How is this different?",
            "content": "<p>Every method you've tried treated smoking as a nicotine problem. So they gave you... more nicotine. Different delivery, same drug.</p><p><strong>Lio treats smoking as a ritual problem.</strong></p><p>Patches stick to your arm while you sit there with empty hands. Gum makes you look like a nervous wreck in meetings. Vaping just trades one addiction for another.</p><p>Lio lets you keep the ritual - the hand motion, the breathing, the sensory experience - while removing the poison.</p><p>You're not fighting your brain anymore. You're giving it what it actually wants: the pattern, the pause, the sensation. Just without the 7,000 chemicals.</p><p><strong>That's why people who failed with everything else succeed with this.</strong> Not because Lio is stronger. Because it's solving a different problem.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_rrCW3H": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "category": "product",
            "title": "What does flavored air actually taste like?",
            "content": "<p>Honest answer: If you're expecting massive clouds and candy vapor, this isn't that.</p><p>Lio tastes like breathing clean air that happens to taste really good. More like inhaling peppermint tea steam than vaping dessert.</p><p>You get:</p><ul><li>Crisp, clean flavor on your tongue</li><li>Subtle throat sensation (especially menthol)</li><li>Real plant taste, not artificial sweetness</li></ul><p>If vaping is sticky soda, Lio is herbal tea. Not as \"strong\" at first, but also not landing you in a hospital.</p><p><strong>What most people say:</strong> <em>\"Didn't think this would be enough. Then my cravings just... disappeared.\"</em></p><p>The flavor satisfies the ritual your brain needs - without the garbage your lungs don't.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_hA4KUD": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "category": "general",
            "title": "How do I return my Lio?",
            "content": "<p><strong>For unused returns (within 14 days):</strong><br/><br/>Email <a href=\"mailto:support@breathelio.com\">support@breathelio.com</a> with your order number. We'll send return instructions. You pay return shipping.</p><p><strong>For 30-day trial refunds:</strong><br/><br/>Email <a href=\"mailto:support@breathelio.com\">support@breathelio.com</a> after completing 30 days with:</p><ul><li>Your order number</li><li>Completed habit tracker (photo or include in package)</li><li>Brief note about your experience</li></ul><p>Refund processes within 2-3 business days. Money hits your account 5-7 days later depending on your bank.</p><p><strong>Important:</strong> Refunds only go back to your original payment method.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_LDAeab": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "category": "general",
            "title": "What's your return policy?",
            "content": "<p><strong>Unused Product (14 days):</strong><br/><br/>Haven't opened it? Return within 14 days of delivery for a full refund. You cover return shipping, and any label fees get deducted from your refund.</p><p><strong>Used Product (30-day trial):</strong><br/><br/>We want you to actually try Lio for 30 days, that's how long it takes to break the ritual. After your 30-day journey, you have 1 extra week to request a refund if it didn't work.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_xjy6Hj": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "category": "general",
            "title": "Can I track my order?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. You'll get a tracking link via email as soon as your order ships.</p><p>Lost the email? Check your spam folder first. Still can't find it? Email <a href=\"mailto:support@breathelio.com\">support@breathelio.com</a> with your order number.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_kBFJWL": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "category": "general",
            "title": "How much is shipping?",
            "content": "<p><strong>Free on all orders.</strong> No minimum. No tricks.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_yfDhXK": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "category": "general",
            "title": "Do you offer bulk/wholesale pricing?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. We work with:</p><ul><li>Quit-smoking clinics</li><li>Corporate wellness programs</li><li>Retail stores</li><li>Health practitioners</li></ul><p>Apply by <a href=\"https://tally.so/r/wogk7M\" title=\"https://tally.so/r/wogk7M\">clicking here</a></p>"
          }
        },
        "question_KaYVrB": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "category": "product",
            "title": "This seems too simple. Can it really work for actual addiction?",
            "content": "<p>Complex problems don't always need complex solutions. They need solutions that address the <em>real</em> problem.</p><p>The quit-smoking industry told you the problem was nicotine. So they gave you nicotine patches, gum, lozenges - just different nicotine. You still failed. Not because you're weak - because they solved the wrong problem.</p><p><strong>The real problem?</strong> After 15 years, stress = cigarette. Coffee = cigarette. Your hand reaches for your pocket before your brain catches up. That's not a nicotine problem. That's a ritual problem.</p><p>Lio works because it replaces the ritual without requiring superhuman willpower. You don't change your life - you just change what you're holding.</p><p><em>\"62 years old, smoked for 30 years... haven't craved my vape at all since using Lio.\"</em></p><p>Sometimes the solution really is simpler than you think.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
